# Day 17 - AI-Powered Vehicle Cost Analysis Dashboard

## Overview

Today I built a Vehicle Cost Analysis Dashboard using Claude AI, a CSV dataset, and customized vehicle information.

The objective was to transform raw vehicle and fuel-related data into a visually appealing, interactive HTML dashboard that provides actionable insights on ownership costs, fuel efficiency, maintenance expenses, and environmental impact.

---

## Objective

Create a complete dashboard capable of analyzing:

* Fuel Cost per Kilometer
* Monthly Running Cost
* Maintenance Expenses
* Vehicle Age Impact
* Environmental Impact
* Alternative Fuel Economics
* E85 Break-Even Analysis

---

## Vehicle Information Used

| Parameter        | Value                                 |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| Vehicle          | Tata Sierra Adventure Plus Turbo 2026 |
| Fuel Type        | Petrol                                |
| Usage            | City                                  |
| Monthly Distance | 1000 KM                               |
| Vehicle Age      | 3 Years                               |

---

## Dashboard Features

### KPI Cards

The dashboard automatically calculated:

* Cost per KM
* Monthly Fuel Cost
* Maintenance Cost per KM
* E85 Cost Comparison
* Break-Even Fuel Price

---

### Interactive Visualizations

#### Fuel Cost Comparison

Compared:

* Petrol
* Diesel
* CNG
* EV
* E85

to identify cost efficiency across fuel types.

---

#### CO₂ Emission Analysis

Visualized environmental impact using:

* CO₂ per KM
* Fuel-based emission comparisons
* Sustainability metrics

---

#### Vehicle Age Analysis

Analyzed:

* Cost per KM by vehicle age
* Maintenance cost growth
* Age bucket comparisons

Buckets Included:

* New (0–2 Years)
* Mid-Life (3–5 Years)
* Aged (6–9 Years)
* Old (10+ Years)

---

### E85 Economics Analysis

The dashboard calculated:

#### Pump Savings

Percentage savings at fuel stations compared to petrol.

#### Running Cost Penalty

Impact of mileage differences on total ownership costs.

#### Break-Even Price

Price point where E85 becomes economically comparable to petrol.

#### E85 Score

Scored fuel viability based on:

* Cost Efficiency
* CO₂ Impact
* Refueling Time
* Maintenance Costs

---

## Key Findings

### Fuel Economics

* Fuel choice significantly impacts long-term ownership costs.
* Running costs vary substantially across fuel types.
* Vehicle age influences maintenance expenses more than fuel expenses.

### Environmental Impact

* Lower emissions do not always result in lower operating costs.
* Sustainability and economics must be evaluated together.

### Ownership Costs

* Monthly running costs are strongly influenced by fuel efficiency and usage patterns.
* Maintenance expenses increase gradually as vehicle age increases.

